[h1]EoE + Immersive Toponyms[/h1]

Compatibility patch for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3679840613]Embers of Empire - A Roman Restoration[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2255229872]Immersive Toponyms[/url].

[h2]Let The Map Tell The Story[/h2]

As borders move and cultures return, the names on the map should move with them. This patch combines EoE's restored Roman realms with the rich regional names from Immersive Toponyms, keeping new titles in place while allowing the map to reflect the world around them.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Latest Update - Version 1.18.3[/h2]

[list]
[*]Updated shared titles for the current EoE and Immersive Toponyms versions.
[*]Refreshed Hungarian place-name references while preserving their accented display names.
[*]Updated compatibility and load-order guidance for CK3 1.19.
[/list]
[hr][/hr]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]

[list]
[*]Embers of Empire - A Roman Restoration
[*]Immersive Toponyms
[/list]

[h2]Load Order[/h2]

[list=1]
[*]Embers of Empire
[*]Immersive Toponyms
[*][b]EoE + Immersive Toponyms[/b]
[/list]

[b]Supported CK3 version:[/b] 1.19.0.6 "Scribe"

Keep this patch after both parent mods and start a new campaign after major updates. If a realm loses its name or a title disappears from the map, report your complete playset, load order, and CK3 version.
